{
  "_readme": [
    "The mission pool. 08-progression.md §7.1 lists 18 canonical dailies and §8.1 lists",
    "10 weeklies; every one of those sentences is below, compiled into the small",
    "objective vocabulary in src/game/missions/types.ts.",
    "",
    "TARGETS ARE THE DESIGN'S, NOT TUNED HERE. The numbers come straight from the two",
    "tables. For reference, a casual AI-vs-AI match measures roughly: 10.5 cards played,",
    "8.7 drawn, 4.7 enemy characters defeated, 34 damage to the enemy leader, 4 Obsession",
    "gained, 1 Fixation, 1.5 elemental bonus hits and 1 card costing 6+. So most dailies",
    "land inside the design's '1-3 matches of natural play'. Two are deck-dependent and",
    "will be slower for a player who does not build for them: 'Fit Check' (Equipment) and",
    "'Weather Report' (Confluences, which the AI rarely activates and a human chooses).",
    "",
    "ALL TEN WEEKLIES NOW SHIP. 'Understudy Arc' and 'Second Bias' were held back until",
    "the Mastery tracks in §4 and §5 existed, because a mission whose condition is always",
    "true pays out for nothing. They read the rank STAMPED ON THE MATCH at play time",
    "(MatchOutcome.masteryAtPlay), not the account's rank today - the rank climbs while you",
    "play, so scoring against today's rank would make finished matches stop counting and a",
    "half-finished mission walk backwards. An outcome carrying no stamp never qualifies."
  ],
  "daily": [
